{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>I made</b>. גן (garden) is masculine: גן נעול (a locked garden), and feminine: לעבדה ולשמרה (to work it and to keep it). The plural is גנים and גנות. The גן contains many trees of many species, while the פרדס (orchard) is of one species — the proof is פרדס רמונים (an orchard of pomegranates)."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:46.746802122Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}